# Economy simulation

- Read docs/PLAN.md and docs/model.md before changing simulation behavior.
- Implement only the phase named in the task. Do not start a later phase.
- When a design decision changes, update docs/PLAN.md and docs/model.md in the same change.
- Write tests first for ledger, accounting, and regime logic.
- Keep functions small. Agents decide in decide() and act through the ledger and markets. They do not modify other agents directly.
- Keep every tunable number in the slider registry. No unexplained constants in agent code.
- Do not add a dependency without noting why.
- Fiat money is integer cents. Bitcoin money is floating-point satoshis, including fractions of a satoshi.
